+Stage 3 — clean reconstruction (bounded command log)
+
+Scratch began with copied source only; candidate runtime-kompiled,
+verification-kompiled, __pycache__, logs, and caches were not copied.
+
+COMMAND
+  cd /tmp/audit-work/reconstruction
+  kompile --backend llvm reference-semantics/semantics.k --main-module MPY-KRUN --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX --output-definition audit-runtime-kompiled
+EXIT
+  0
+RELEVANT OUTPUT
+  Warnings only: non-exhaustive unused fixed helpers mapStrVS, floorFI, toF,
+  ceilF, joinCodes, valSeqAt; unused As/Bs in strLt. No error.
+
+COMMAND
+  for n in 0 1 2 5 10; do
+    python3 make_smoke.py "$n" > "audit-smoke-$n.mpy"
+    krun "audit-smoke-$n.mpy" --definition audit-runtime-kompiled --output pretty > "audit-smoke-$n.out"
+  done
+EXIT
+  all five krun invocations: 0
+RELEVANT OUTPUT
+  n=0:  0 |-> list ( .ValSeq )
+  n=1:  0 |-> list ( vCons ( 1 , .ValSeq ) )
+  n=2:  0 |-> list ( vCons ( 1 , vCons ( 2 , .ValSeq ) ) )
+  n=5:  0 |-> list ( vCons ( 1 , vCons ( 2 , vCons ( 6 , vCons ( 24 , vCons ( 15 , .ValSeq ) ) ) ) ) )
+  n=10: 0 |-> list ( vCons ( 1 , vCons ( 2 , vCons ( 6 , vCons ( 24 , vCons ( 15 , vCons ( 720 , vCons ( 28 , vCons ( 40320 , vCons ( 45 , vCons ( 3628800 , .ValSeq ) ) ) ) ) ) ) ) ) ) )
+  Every run ended with stack .List, ret noRet, exc NoExc, exit-code 0.
+
+COMMAND
+  kompile --backend haskell verification.k --main-module VERIFICATION --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX --output-definition audit-verification-kompiled
+EXIT
+  0
+RELEVANT OUTPUT
+  Only the four pre-existing unused-variable warnings in str.k.
+
+COMMAND
+  kprove spec.k --definition audit-verification-kompiled --spec-module SPEC --claims SPEC.loop-invariant
+EXIT
+  0
+OUTPUT
+  #Top
+  (followed only by the four str.k unused-variable warnings)
+
+COMMAND
+  kprove spec.k --definition audit-verification-kompiled --spec-module SPEC
+EXIT
+  0
+OUTPUT
+  #Top
+  (followed only by the four str.k unused-variable warnings)
+
+The full command is the positive proof suite and closes both
+SPEC.loop-invariant and SPEC.f-correct together. A diagnostic command selecting
+only SPEC.f-correct exits 1 at the first loop iteration because selection also
+removes the auxiliary loop circularity. Its residual is
+  vCons(1,.ValSeq) = resultRun(.ValSeq,1,N,1,0)
+under 1 <= N and not 2 <= N. This is expected dependency evidence, not a
+failure of the full two-claim reachability proof.
